media/gpu/v4l2: treat an error CAPTURE buffer as a decode error

The stateless backend marked every dequeued CAPTURE buffer decoded and
output it, including buffers the driver returned with V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR
(a picture it refused or that failed in hardware). Playback then showed
blank frames and counted them as decoded. Report a backend error instead.

--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder_backend_stateless.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_video_decoder_backend_stateless.cc
@@ -200,6 +200,16 @@
   DCHECK_EQ(static_cast<size_t>(surface->output_record()),
             dequeued_buffer->BufferId());
   surfaces_at_device_.pop();
+
+  // A driver that could not decode the picture returns its buffer with
+  // V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR. Showing that buffer would show a picture that was
+  // never decoded (a blank or stale frame) while playback looks healthy;
+  // report a decode error instead so the pipeline can fall back.
+  if (dequeued_buffer->IsError()) {
+    LOG(ERROR) << "The driver failed to decode a picture";
+    client_->OnBackendError();
+    return;
+  }
 
   surface->SetDecoded();
 
